          <msContents>
            <summary>This manuscript is a Socratic dialogue by the Roman philosopher, Cicero.
              <b>Contents:</b>
              <p>Fol. 1v 'MAGISTRI TYGRINI Mcccclxxxvii', in very faded ink. </p>
              <p>2 Dicteria septem sapientium. Ten lines of Greek verse, with Latin translation of the words written above. </p>
              <p>2v 'Infracscriptum jusjurandum scriptum est in lapide vetustissimo in creta ad opidum [sic] scithie', followed by 8 lines of the Greek text. </p>
              <p>Below 'Transcriptum per me hieronymum Tygrinum. Ex quodem codice Nicolai Feretti preceptoris anno 1497 octubris lucce. </p>
              <p>3 (red) Marci Tullii Cicernis de finibus bonorum et malorum //Liber primus incipit feliciter. //NOS ERAM NESCIVS BRVTE/ quumque summis ingeniis...</p>
              <p>87 ...ad pomponium porreximus /omnes. //(red) M. Tullii Ciceronis de finibus bonorum et malorum liber/quintus et ultimus explicit feliciter.</p>
              <p>89v 'Est mei hieronymi tygrini tiberiachiensis', and the date 1500.</p>
            </summary>
            <textLang mainLang="la" source="IANA">Latin</textLang>
            <msItem n="1" xml:id="MS_195_1">
              <author>Cicero (Marcus Tullius) (106-43 B.C.)</author>
              <title type="original" xml:lang="la">De finibus bonorum et malorum</title>
              <title type="standard" xml:lang="en">On the ends of good and evil</title>
              <textLang mainLang="ka" source="IANA">Latin</textLang>
              <textLang otherLangs="grc" source="IANA">Ancient Greek</textLang>
            </msItem>
          </msContents>
